{
  "answer_text": "The method that achieves the lowest hallucination rate within each paper is as follows:\n\n*   **S001:** Chain-of-thought prompting (9.4%) [S001, 2088-2166].\n*   **S006:** Fine-tuned model (9.8%) [S006, 2328-2399].\n*   **S007:** Generator adapted to the domain by further training (18.2%) [S007, 3021-3172].\n*   **S008:** Retrieval-augmented generator (6.3%) [S008, 2598-2656].\n*   **S010:** RAG without reranking (23.1%) [S010, 2143-2285].\n*   **S012:** Model that answers from its own parameters (19.3%) [S012, 2463-2606].\n*   **S016:** Retrieval-augmented generator (5.1%) [S016, 2391-2484].\n*   **S017:** Model that samples several answers and votes (19.1%) [S017, 2809-2943].\n*   **S018:** Retrieve-then-read model (16.3%) [S018, 2705-2760].\n\nNote: Papers S002, S003, S004, S005, S009, S011, S013, S014, S015, S019, and S020 do not report hallucination rate as their primary metric (they use fact-level accuracy, answer accuracy, or other metrics), so they are excluded from this specific comparison.",
